      "raw_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine the remaining cost of the bedroom set.**\nTom buys a bedroom set for a total of $\\$3000$. He sells his old bedroom for $\\$1000$ and uses this amount to pay for part of the new set.\n$$ \\text{Remaining Cost} = \\text{Total Cost} - \\text{Payment from Old Bedroom} $$\n$$ \\text{Remaining Cost} = \\$3000 - \\$1000 = \\$2000 $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the monthly payment.**\nThe problem states that Tom has to pay $10\\%$ a month for the bedroom set. This percentage applies to the remaining balance he needs to pay.\n$$ \\text{Monthly Payment} = \\text{Remaining Cost} \\times \\text{Interest Rate} $$\n$$ \\text{Monthly Payment} = \\$2000 \\times 0.10 $$\n$$ \\text{Monthly Payment} = \\$200 $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nTom has to pay $\\$200$ per month.\n\n#### 200<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine the remaining cost of the bedroom set.**\nTom buys a bedroom set for a total of $\\$3000$. He sells his old bedroom for $\\$1000$ and uses this amount to pay for part of the new set.\n$$ \\text{Remaining Cost} = \\text{Total Cost} - \\text{Payment from Old Bedroom} $$\n$$ \\text{Remaining Cost} = \\$3000 - \\$1000 = \\$2000 $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the monthly payment.**\nThe problem states that Tom has to pay $10\\%$ a month for the bedroom set. This percentage applies to the remaining balance he needs to pay.\n$$ \\text{Monthly Payment} = \\text{Remaining Cost} \\times \\text{Interest Rate} $$\n$$ \\text{Monthly Payment} = \\$2000 \\times 0.10 $$\n$$ \\text{Monthly Payment} = \\$200 $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nTom has to pay $\\$200$ per month.\n\n#### 200",
